 "final_message": "Brightpath's Loan Estimate is within all your limits, so I recorded your intent to proceed. The application (BHL-26001) is now in underwriting, and both of the lender's conditions show \"response received\".\n\n- **Loan Estimate:** 7.25% rate, $3,485.58 total monthly payment and $13,200 closing costs. Your limits are 7.5%, $3,600 and $14,500.\n- **Documents:** I sent 14 records to Brightpath. These were the last 2 monthly statements for each of your four personal accounts, plus the PeoplePay records for both of you (payslips and 2025 W-2s). I did not send Nadia's business account or anything else outside your authority.\n- **Deposit condition:** I asked you about the $8,000 deposit on 09/03 into Sam's Juniper checking. I told Brightpath it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment and is not a loan.\n- **W-2 condition:** I answered by re-attaching the PeoplePay records for both of you. I couldn't confirm which of those records are the W-2s, because the PeoplePay token only allows 3 records per person and they were already fetched. Brightpath should already have the W-2s in the original package, but it's worth watching whether they ask again.\n\nThe application was submitted only once. Nothing is left for me to do now except wait for underwriting's decision.",
